L1193: 10.1 CONFIDENTIALITY OF PARTICIPANT RECORDS
L1194: Participants will be identified by a study identification number. It will be necessary to collect the
L1195: participants name and contact information as this study will require several scheduling procedures. This
L1196: information will be kept separate from the participant study identification number.
L1197: **11. ADMINISTRATIVE REQUIREMENTS**
L1198: 11.1 PROTOCOL AMENDMENTS
L1199: The leaders of the study, in collaboration with members of the team, may modify the protocol at any
L1200: time during the study. Protocol amendments will require REB approval prior to implementation of any
L1201: changes.
L1202: 11.2 COMPLETION OF CASE REPORT FORMS (CRFS)
L1203: All sites participating in his study will be trained on completion of CRFs. The primary investigators at
L1204: all sites are responsible for the CRFs with respect to completeness, accuracy, and clarity.
L1205: 11.3 MONITORING PROCEDURES
L1206: All sites will use the same data collection forms to maintain consistency. Monitoring procedures will be
L1207: performed using the LORIS system platform for uploading data specially developed for the SYNERGIC
L1208: study by CCNA informatics team platform.
L1209: **12. PUBLICATION POLICY**
L1210: The SYNERGIC Trial will follow CCNA publication policy.
