L1496: 1
L1497: SYNERGIC Trial                                                    Statistical Analyses Plan
L1498: ## 31 1. Introduction
L1499: 32 The SYNERGIC TRIAL (SYNchronizing Exercises, Remedies in GaIt and Cognition) is
L1500: 33 a randomized, phase II, fractional factorial, five-arm, double-blind controlled study
L1501: 34 evaluating the effect of aerobic-resistance exercise with and without cognitive training
L1502: 35 and vitamin D supplementation on cognitive function.
L1503: 36 Specifically, physical exercise is a progressive and supervised aerobic (AE) and
L1504: 37 resistance training (RT) program tailored for older adults’ physical capabilities.
L1505: 38 Computerized cognitive training will be delivered using the Neuropeak cognitive training
L1506: 39 program designed to target working memory and attention. Vitamin D supplementation
L1507: 40 will be delivered in capsules with 10,000 IU, 3 times per week, reaching a weekly dose
L1508: 41 of 30000 IU. Control interventions will be sham cognitive training, balance and toning
L1509: 42 exercise (BAT), and matching vitamin D placebo capsules.
L1510: 43
L1511: ## 44 2. Study Objectives
L1512: 45 To evaluate:
L1513: 46 **Objective 1** The effect of supervised aerobic-resistance exercise on cognitive function
L1514: 47 **Hypothesis 1.** Twenty weeks of supervised aerobic-resistance exercise will significantly
L1515: 48 improve cognitive function in older adults with MCI, as assessed by primary outcome
L1516: 49 Alzheimer’s Disease Assessment Scale-Cognitive (ADAS-Cog 13 and plus variant) and
L1517: 50 secondary outcomes, compared to a balance and toning (BAT) control.
L1518: 51 **Objective 2.** The effect of adding cognitive training to aerobic-resistance exercise on
L1519: 52 cognitive function.
L1520: 53 **Hypothesis 2.** Adding cognitive training to aerobic-resistance exercise will significantly
L1521: 54 improve primary and secondary outcomes compared to aerobic-resistance exercise
L1522: 55 without cognitive training.
L1523: 56 **Objective 3.** The effect of adding vitamin D supplementation to aerobic-resistance
L1524: 57 exercise on cognitive function.
L1525: 58 **Hypothesis 3.** Adding vitamin D supplementation in weekly dose of 30000 IU to
L1526: 59 aerobic-resistance exercise will significantly improve primary and secondary outcomes
L1527: 60 compared to aerobic-resistance exercise without vitamin D supplementation.
L1528: 61 **Objective 4.** The effect of multi-domain intervention (aerobic-resistance exercise +
L1529: 62 cognitive training + Vitamin D supplementation) on cognitive function.
L1530: 63 **Hypothesis 4.** The multi-domain intervention (aerobic-resistance exercise + cognitive
L1531: 64 training + vitamin D supplementation) will significantly improve primary and secondary
L1532: 65 outcomes compared to the control intervention.
L1533: 2
L1534: SYNERGIC Trial                                                    Statistical Analyses Plan
L1535: 66
L1536: ## 67 3. Study Population
L1537: 68 We will target older adults aged 60 to 85 years old with mild cognitive impairment (MCI).
L1538: 69
L1539: ## 70 4. Study Design
L1540: 71 This is a Phase II, randomized, double-blind, five-arm controlled trial. The trial design
L1541: 72 follows a fractional factorial design as shown in Figure 1. Participants will be recruited
L1542: 73 primarily from the community and from clinics serving MCI population across five sites:
L1543: 74 London (lead and sponsor site), Waterloo-University of Waterloo, Waterloo-Wilfrid
L1544: 75 Laurier University, Montreal, and Vancouver. All eligible participants will be randomized
L1545: 76 to 5 arms in 1:1:1:1:1 ratio:
L1546: 77 Arm 1: combined AE and RT exercise + cognitive training + vitamin D
L1547: 78 Arm 2: combined AE and RT exercise + cognitive training + placebo vitamin D
L1548: 79 Arm 3: combined AE and RT exercise + control cognitive training + vitamin D
L1549: 80 Arm 4: combined AE and RT exercise + control cognitive training+ placebo vitamin D
L1550: 81 Arm 5: BAT exercise + control cognitive training + placebo vitamin D
L1551: 82
L1552: 83 Figure 1. Trial design overview
L1553: ## 84 5. Study Endpoint
L1554: 85 The study endpoint will be at 6 Month (post-intervention).
L1555: 3
L1556: SYNERGIC Trial                                                    Statistical Analyses Plan
L1557: 86
L1558: ## 87 6. Study Assessment
L1559: 88 The participant’s eligibility will be assessed during the screening visit. Assessment
L1560: 89 which will be performed during three visits: baseline, post-intervention at 6 months, and
L1561: 90 6-month follow up after the postintervention at 12 months. The measures at each
L1562: 91 assessment are described in Table 1.
L1563: 92
